# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MISERY Modding Framework -- .gitignore
#
# Guiding principle: this repository's value is DIFFABLE TEXT. Anything that is
# (a) a copy of a game binary, (b) rebuildable from text we already track, or
# (c) machine/editor noise, stays out of git.
#
# Derived artifacts are ignored because they are REBUILDABLE from the JSONL
# sources, and the JSONL stays in git precisely so it can be diffed between
# builds. A SQLite database cannot be reviewed in a pull request; a JSONL line
# can. If a derived artifact ever stops being rebuildable, that is a bug in the
# tool, not a reason to commit the artifact.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------


# --- workspace: binary copies, Ghidra projects, large dumps ----------------
# Per plan.md 1.5 layer 2, every binary that a writing-capable tool must open is
# first COPIED into workspace/bin/. Those copies are multi-hundred-megabyte
# game files -- never committed. Ghidra projects and raw dumps live here too.
# The directory itself is kept (see the .gitkeep exception below) so that the
# layout survives a fresh clone and no tool has to mkdir before it can run.
workspace/*
!workspace/bin
workspace/bin/*
!workspace/bin/.gitkeep


# --- game binaries and containers: NEVER commit ----------------------------
# Belt and braces on top of the workspace rule. These extensions can only ever
# appear in this repository by accident (a stray copy, a wrong output path, a
# careless drag-and-drop). Committing game content would be both useless for
# research and a distribution problem. If one of these is genuinely needed as
# evidence, record its sha256 and size in a JSON artifact instead of the file.
*.utoc
*.ucas
*.pak
*.exe
*.dll
*.pdb
*.usmap
*.uasset
*.umap
*.uexp
*.ubulk


# --- derived databases: rebuildable from tracked JSONL ---------------------
# reflection.sqlite is produced by tools/kb/build_sqlite.py from the JSONL files
# in the same directory (plan.md K-04, and 9.2 marks it gitignore explicitly).
# The JSONL is the source of truth and is tracked; the database is a query
# convenience that can be regenerated at any time.
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db
research/reflection/*/reflection.sqlite


# --- Ghidra project artifacts ----------------------------------------------
# A Ghidra project is a mutable working state (analysis results, user markup,
# lock files), not a research finding. Findings are exported to research/ as
# text by pyghidra_scripts/. Project roots live under D:\Tools\ghidra-projects
# by design, but a stray project inside the repo must not be committed either.
*.gpr
*.rep/
*.lock
*.gzf
ghidra_*.log


# --- Python bytecode and virtual environments ------------------------------
# Bytecode is generated from tracked sources. Virtual environments are
# machine-specific, huge, and reconstructed from requirements.txt -- committing
# one would pin absolute Windows paths into the repository.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/


# --- generated stub trees (plan.md 14A) ------------------------------------
# research/modkit/generated-stubs/ holds C++ headers synthesised from the
# reflection dump. They are fully derived from research/reflection/<build_key>/
# and can be enormous (one header per UClass). Policy: a SMALL, hand-curated
# subset may be committed as evidence for a specific finding; a full generated
# tree may not. Un-comment the line below the moment the tree stops being
# reviewable in a diff -- and record that decision in research/decisions.md.
# research/modkit/generated-stubs/**
research/modkit/generated-stubs/*.zip
research/modkit/generated-stubs/*.7z
research/modkit/generated-stubs/*.tar.gz


# --- large raw dumps -------------------------------------------------------
# Instrument runs and evidence directories can accumulate multi-gigabyte raw
# captures. Keep the text summary, drop the raw blob; reference the blob by
# sha256 and by the workspace path where it was produced.
*.bin
*.dmp
*.raw
*.zip
*.7z
*.tar.gz


# --- OS noise --------------------------------------------------------------
# Created by Explorer / Finder, carry no information, and cause phantom diffs.
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store


# --- editor noise ----------------------------------------------------------
# Per-developer IDE state. Shared configuration, if it ever becomes necessary,
# should be added deliberately with a negation rule and a comment.
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~

# .NET build output for the public mod API contracts. The SOURCE is the
# deliverable; bin/ and obj/ are regenerated by `dotnet build` and would
# otherwise commit a compiled assembly plus a NuGet lock graph on every build.
managed/**/bin/
managed/**/obj/
